1236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (If firms are producing less goods and services, they may need fewer workers. This can result in a rise in cyclical unemployment. Some of the workers who lose their jobs may lose their skills and confidence and so may find it difficult to find other jobs when economic activity picks up. A reduction in investment would also reduce productive capacity. This again could result in a decrease in output as shown in the diagram. In this case both aggregate demand and aggregate supply decrease.)
/E (If firms are producing less goods and services, they may need fewer workers. This can result in a rise in cyclical unemployment. Some of the workers who lose their jobs may lose their skills and confidence and so may find it difficult to find other jobs when economic activity picks up. A reduction in investment would also reduce productive capacity. This again could result in a decrease in output as shown in the diagram. In this case both aggregate demand and aggregate supply decrease.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [7]
>>
