/T (Total Using Fig.1, explain the relationship between changes in consumer expenditure and changes in income. Direct/positive relationship between consumer expenditure and income/rise in income results in a rise in consumer expenditure \(1\). The proportion of income spent falls as income rises/average propensity to consume falls as income rises \(1\). At low levels of income, people spend more than their income/ there is dissaving/people spend savings/benefits \(1\) Gradient decreases as it becomes more attractive to save \(1\))
/E (Total Using Fig.1, explain the relationship between changes in consumer expenditure and changes in income. Direct/positive relationship between consumer expenditure and income/rise in income results in a rise in consumer expenditure \(1\). The proportion of income spent falls as income rises/average propensity to consume falls as income rises \(1\). At low levels of income, people spend more than their income/ there is dissaving/people spend savings/benefits \(1\) Gradient decreases as it becomes more attractive to save \(1\))
